# Docs prose

When writing or editing user-facing copy (intros, section descriptions, demos, metadata descriptions):

- Do not use em dashes (`—`) or en dashes (`–`). Prefer a period and a new sentence, or a colon when introducing a list or clarification.
- Use commas only when grammar requires them (lists of three or more, or to prevent misreading). Prefer shorter sentences over comma-heavy clauses.
- Prefer short sentences that scan easily. Cut filler.
- Keep empty-value placeholders in props tables as `—` (UI convention, not prose).
